# io-mcp cron examples (alternative to the systemd timer).
#
# Install with:  crontab -e   (paste the lines below, fixing the venv path)
# Prefer the systemd timer (deploy/io-mcp-digest.timer) on Fedora; use cron only
# if you'd rather not deal with user units.
#
# Replace /path/to/io-mcp/.venv with your actual environment. For a conda env:
#   ~/miniconda3/envs/io-mcp/bin/io-mcp

# Run the paper digest at 06:00 every day.
0 6 * * * /path/to/io-mcp/.venv/bin/io-mcp digest

# Weekly: prune seen-paper state older than 90 days (Sundays at midnight).
0 0 * * 0 /path/to/io-mcp/.venv/bin/io-mcp digest --dry-run --prune-days 90
